<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tips - Category | Boy's Life</title><link>https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/categories/tips/</link><description>独立开发者 Travis Bikkle 的个人博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.138.0 &amp; FixIt v0.3.15-fd15415b</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>travisbikkle@proton.me (Travis Bikkle)</managingEditor><webMaster>travisbikkle@proton.me (Travis Bikkle)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Tue, 12 Nov 2024 11:53:31 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/categories/tips/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Transform SCWindow coordinate</title><link>https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/2024/10/how-did-i-develop-mactoys-pin-window/</link><pubDate>Mon, 21 Oct 2024 11:24:35 +0800</pubDate><author>travisbikkle@proton.me (Travis Bikkle)</author><guid>https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/2024/10/how-did-i-develop-mactoys-pin-window/</guid><category domain="https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/categories/tips/">Tips</category><description>&lt;p>(Translated)&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The coordinate system we use most is the standard Cartesian plane right-angle coordinate system, which takes the lower-left corner of the screen as the origin and increases the y coordinate upwards and the x coordinate to the right.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>SCWindow&amp;rsquo;s coordinates, on the other hand, are flipped coordinates with the upper-left corner of the main screen as the origin, and the following is a simple comparison chart:&lt;/p>
